From c933d51b98876c9e27905cbae50da3a12be350b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:18:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add Hila's updated APOL1, Uncertain Results/VUS and How to
 Get Tested content

APOL1
- New title "APOL1 risk factor" and subtitle on AMKD; new explanation of
  APOL1, G1/G2 and recessive risk, with the APOL1 variants figure.
- "Most (~80%) people with 2 variants do NOT develop kidney disease"
  callout and a Definitions box (genotype, high-risk genotype).
- Heading renamed "A note on kidney transplantation" (per Hila's comment).
- For more information: NKF, AAKP, American Kidney Fund, NephCure, and
  Alonzo Mourning's story (tracking parameters removed from the link).

Uncertain Results / VUS
- New title "Understanding your genetic test report" and VUS subtitle.
- Positive vs Negative explained side by side, with the positive vs
  negative result figure; VUS definition and "should NOT be used to make
  medical decisions" callout; kept GenomeConnect, underrepresented
  backgrounds and Types of tests paragraphs with their citations.

How to Get Tested
- New title "How can I get genetic testing?"; new sections: The path to
  the test (links to Genetic counselors and the Genetic Risk Check),
  What do I need to do to meet with a genetic counselor?, Is genetic
  testing covered by insurance? (FAQ text plus Hila's additions), and
  Additional information (American Kidney Fund, NephCure). Kept the
  questions to ask your care team.

FAQ
- Referral and cost answers shortened to one or two lines that link to
  the matching How to Get Tested section, instead of repeating it.
- APOL1 and VUS answers updated to Hila's new wording.

Search index refreshed.

